fuse_abort_conn(fc, false);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `fuse_dev_release()` assumes it is the only function accessing the `fpq->processing` list. However, `fuse_abort_conn()` can also access this list concurrently without proper synchronization, leading to potential race conditions when both functions manipulate the list simultaneously.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
spin_lock(&fpq->lock);
list_splice_init(&fpq->processing, &to_end);
spin_unlock(&fpq->lock);
end_requests(fc, &to_end);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a spin lock around the access to `fpq->processing`, ensuring that only one function can manipulate the list at a time. This prevents concurrent access by `fuse_abort_conn()` and `fuse_dev_release()`, thus eliminating the race condition and ensuring safe manipulation of the list.

